{number: 104}
{title: My Jesus, I Love Thee}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
My [C] Jesus, I [F] love Thee, I [C] know Thou art [G7] mine;
For [C] Thee all the [F] follies of [C] sin I re-[G7] [C] sign;
My [C] gracious Re-[F] deemer, my [C] Savior art [G7] Thou;
If [C] ever I [F] loved Thee, my [C] Jesus, [G7] 'tis [C] now.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
I [C] love Thee be-[F] cause Thou hast [C] first loved [G7] me,
And [C] purchased my [F] pardon on [C] Calvary's [G7] [C] tree;
I [C] love Thee for [F] wearing the [C] thorns on Thy [G7] brow;
If [C] ever I [F] loved Thee, my [C] Jesus, [G7] 'tis [C] now.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
I'll [C] love Thee in [F] life, I will [C] love Thee in [G7] death,
And [C] praise Thee as [F] long as Thou [C] lendest me [G7] [C] breath;
And [C] say when the [F] death dew lies [C] cold on my [G7] brow,
If [C] ever I [F] loved Thee, my [C] Jesus, [G7] 'tis [C] now.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
In [C] mansions of [F] glory and [C] endless de-[G7] light,
I'll [C] ever a-[F] dore Thee in [C] heaven so [G7] [C] bright;
I'll [C] sing with the [F] glittering [C] crown on my [G7] brow,
If [C] ever I [F] loved Thee, my [C] Jesus, [G7] 'tis [C] now.
{end_of_verse}
